<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic down 0.9pct in Jan-Nov 96.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic down 0.9pct in Jan-Nov 96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo exports from the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 537,880 tonnes in the first eleven months of 1996, down 0.9 percent on the same period in 1995, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>Global January-November 1996 export traffic from ADP, by region, with percentage change on January-November 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		 43,119 tonnes  down   0.2pct</p>
<p> European Union	 63,520 tonnes  up     2.9</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	  12,066 tonnes  down   2.3</p>
<p> North Africa	    9,620 tonnes  down  30.5</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa   43,830 tonnes  up     1.4</p>
<p> North America	 148,112 tonnes  down   1.0</p>
<p> French territories   24,268 tonnes  down   4.7</p>
<p> Latin America	  28,476 tonnes  up     4.1</p>
<p> Middle East	    53,327 tonnes  up     7.3</p>
<p> Far East		111,542 tonnes  down   4.0</p>
<p> Total		   537,880 tonnes  down   0.9</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
